'''''Crescentia''''' ('''calabash tree''', '''huingo''', '''krabasi''', or '''kalebas''') is a genus of six species<ref>{{cite web
 |url         = http://www.ars-grin.gov/cgi-bin/npgs/html/splist.pl?3069
 |publisher   = Germplasm Resources Information Network
 |title       = Crescentia
 |access-date  = 2011-09-24
 |url-status     = dead
 |archive-url  = https://web.archive.org/web/20130327221125/http://www.ars-grin.gov/cgi-bin/npgs/html/splist.pl?3069
 |archive-date = 2013-03-27
}}</ref> of [[flowering plant]]s in the family [[Bignoniaceae]], native to Mexico, the [[Caribbean]], [[Central America]], and northern [[South America]].<ref name=powo/> The species are moderate-size [[tree]]s growing to {{convert|10|m|ft|round=5|abbr=on}} tall, and producing large spherical fruits, with a thin, hard shell and soft pulp,<ref name="rainforest">{{cite web
 | title=Crescentia cujete (Huingo)
 | url=http://www.rainforestconservation.org/?s=calabash
 | publisher=Rainforest Conservation Fund
 | access-date=2011-09-24
}}</ref> up to {{convert|25|cm|in|0|abbr=on}} in diameter.<ref>{{cite web
 | url=http://www.missiontobelize.org/node/192
 | title=Calabash Tree Fruit
 | publisher=Mission to Belize
 | access-date=2011-09-24
 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110829185716/http://www.missiontobelize.org/node/192
 | archive-date=2011-08-29
 | url-status=dead
 }}</ref>

==Uses==
The hard shell can be used for containers, scoops, cups etc.<ref name="rainforest" />

==Species==
Six species are accepted.<ref name = powo/>
*''[[Crescentia alata]]'' {{small|Kunth}}
*''[[Crescentia amazonica]]'' {{small|Ducke}}
*''[[Crescentia cujete]]'' {{small|L.}}
*''[[Crescentia linearifolia]]'' {{small|Miers}}
*''[[Crescentia mirabilis]]'' {{small|Eckman ex Urb.}}
*''[[Crescentia portoricensis]]'' {{small|Britton}}

